{"name":"Dark Seagreen","hex":"#666655","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dark","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having an absolute or (more often) relative lack of light.","Extinguished."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A complete or (more often) partial absence of light.","Ignorance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dark"},{"term":"seagreen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The houseleek.","Alternative form of sea green."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seagreen"}],"entries":[{"title":"X11 color names","blocks":[{"text":"In computing, on the X Window System, X11 color names are represented in a simple text file, which maps certain strings to RGB color values. It was traditionally shipped with every X11 installation, hence the name, and is usually located in <X11root>/lib/X11/rgb.txt. The web colors list is descended from it but differs for certain color names."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X11_color_names"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Shades_of_red.png/500px-Shades_of_red.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Shades_of_red.png/500px-Shades_of_red.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShades_of_red.png"}],"sounds":{"dark":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/24/En-us-dark.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/24/En-us-dark.ogg/En-us-dark.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"The Indian grey mongoose (Urva edwardsii) mating 4","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/The_Indian_grey_mongoose_%28Urva_edwardsii%29_mating_4.jpg